      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Closeburn Castle is a tower house, probably of the 14th century, but possibly older, and is one of the oldest continually inhabited houses in Scotland. The castle is located 1 km east of the village of Closeburn, and 2 km south-east of Thornhill, in Dumfries and Galloway, south-west Scotland.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
